      {
        "text": "It repenteth me that I have set up Saul to be king: for he is turned back from following me, and hath not performed my commandments. And it grieved Samuel; and he cried unto the Lord all night.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 2,
            "text": "JST 1 Sam. 15:11 I have set up Saul to be a king, and he repenteth not that he hath sinned, for he is …"
          },
          {
            "start": 3,
            "end": 12,
            "text": "The Hebrew root means “to sigh,” therefore “to feel sorrow.” Gen. 6:6; 2 Sam. 24:16; Joel 2:13."
